{% comment %}
  Global booking flow, triggered from any CTA with class "kal-request-appointment-cta"
  anywhere in the theme. Rendered once in layout/theme.liquid.
  Uses the native <dialog> element so it always renders above all other page
  content, regardless of any CSS transform/stacking-context elsewhere in the theme.
{% endcomment %}

{%- comment -%}
  kal-booking-flow.css cascades a single --kal-booking-flow-font-family: 'Avenir' and
  relies on numeric font-weight (350/400/500/700/800) to pick the right
  cut, unlike the main theme's custom-font.liquid (which declares each
  Avenir weight as its own separate family name). So this flow needs real
  @font-face rules under ONE "Avenir" family instead — declared here,
  inline, the same way custom-font.liquid does it for the main theme,
  since the static .css asset itself can't run the asset_url filter.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% style %}
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Avenir';
    src: url('{{ "Avenir-Light.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 300;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Avenir';
    src: url('{{ "Avenir-Book.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Avenir';
    src: url('{{ "Avenir-Medium.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 500;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  {%- comment -%}
    600 has no dedicated Avenir file — without this, the browser has to
    guess the nearest registered weight (300/400/500/700/800) for any
    font-weight:600 rule, and that guess can silently resolve to a face
    that looks identical to what was there before (e.g. "Calm care,
    closer than you think." showing no visible change after being set to
    600). Explicitly registering 600 against the same Avenir-Medium file
    as 500 makes it an exact match instead, guaranteeing a real font
    change even though it reuses that file's actual weight.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Avenir';
    src: url('{{ "Avenir-Medium.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 600;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Avenir';
    src: url('{{ "Avenir-Heavy.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 700;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Avenir';
    src: url('{{ "Avenir-Black.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 800;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  {%- comment -%}
    900 has no dedicated Avenir file either — reuses Avenir-Black.woff2,
    same pattern as 600 reusing Avenir-Medium.woff2 above, so
    font-weight:900 (option-card primary title) resolves to this face
    instead of the browser guessing/falling back to 800.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Avenir';
    src: url('{{ "Avenir-Black.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 900;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
{% endstyle %}
{{ 'kal-booking-flow.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'kal-booking-flow.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

<dialog
  id="kal-booking-flow"
  class="kal-booking-flow"
  data-api-base-url="{{ settings.kal_booking_api_base_url }}"
  data-whatsapp-number="{{ settings.kal_booking_whatsapp_number }}"
  data-doctor-photo-placeholder="{{ 'kal-doctor-photo-placeholder.jpg' | asset_url }}"
  data-kal-active-step="entry"
>
  {%- comment -%}
    Only visible on Entry (see goToStep() in kal-booking-flow.js — hidden
    on every other step, which render their own close button as part of
    kal-booking-flow-step-header.liquid instead). Reuses that same
    .kal-step-doctor-select__back circular/bordered treatment + 'close'
    icon here too, instead of a plain "×" character, so Entry's close
    button looks the same as every other step's.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <button class="kal-booking-flow__close kal-step-doctor-select__back" data-kal-close aria-label="Close">
    {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'close' -%}
  </button>
  <div class="kal-booking-flow__content" id="kal-booking-flow-content">
    <div data-kal-step="entry">
      {% render 'kal-booking-flow-step-entry' %}
    </div>
    <div data-kal-step="concern-select" hidden>
      {% render 'kal-booking-flow-step-concern-select' %}
    </div>
    <div data-kal-step="doctor-select" hidden>
      {% render 'kal-booking-flow-step-doctor-select' %}
    </div>
    <div data-kal-step="slot-picker" hidden>
      {% render 'kal-booking-flow-step-slot-picker' %}
    </div>
    <div data-kal-step="patient-details" hidden>
      {% render 'kal-booking-flow-step-patient-details' %}
    </div>
    <div data-kal-step="confirmation" hidden>
      {% render 'kal-booking-flow-step-confirmation' %}
    </div>
    <div data-kal-step="booking-confirmed" hidden>
      {% render 'kal-booking-flow-step-booking-confirmed' %}
    </div>
    <div data-kal-step="therapy-slot" hidden>
      {% render 'kal-booking-flow-step-therapy-slot' %}
    </div>
    <div data-kal-step="therapy-details" hidden>
      {% render 'kal-booking-flow-step-therapy-details' %}
    </div>
    <div data-kal-step="therapy-confirmed" hidden>
      {% render 'kal-booking-flow-step-therapy-confirmed' %}
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Facility-switch confirmation — one shared instance for the whole flow,
    not one per header render (kal-booking-flow-step-header.liquid's
    facility dropdown renders 3x, once per switchable step, all
    simultaneously in the DOM). Shown by kal-booking-flow.js's
    openFacilitySwitchModal() when switching clinics on Doctor Select/Slot
    Picker would move away from the currently-selected mock doctor's home
    clinic — doctor/facility name text is filled in by JS right before
    this becomes visible. MOCK data only (see kal-booking-flow.js's
    FACILITY SWITCHER comment) until real per-clinic doctor data replaces
    Doctor Select's 3 static mock doctor cards.

    Both real actions (Change Clinic / Book an online slot) apply the
    facility switch and send the visitor back to Doctor Select (step 2)
    to pick a doctor again — the doctor they had selected was only valid
    for their old clinic/mode combination, not the new one. The only
    difference between the two is which consultation mode Doctor Select
    lands on (in-clinic vs video), via the same setMode() the mode toggle
    buttons there already use. The corner X is the sole "never mind, stay
    on my current clinic" cancel action — no facility switch, no
    navigation.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="kal-facility-switch-modal" data-kal-facility-switch-modal hidden>
    <div class="kal-facility-switch-modal__card">
      <button type="button" class="kal-facility-switch-modal__close" data-kal-facility-switch-cancel aria-label="Close">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'close' -%}
      </button>
      {%- comment -%}
        Photo removed per explicit instruction (flow-wide) — plain
        placeholder box instead of the doctor's photo for now.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <span class="kal-facility-switch-modal__photo">
        <span class="kal-doctor-photo-placeholder"></span>
      </span>
      <p class="kal-facility-switch-modal__text">
        <strong data-kal-facility-switch-doctor>Dr. Neethu Jayachandran</strong> is available in person only at the
        <strong data-kal-facility-switch-facility>Koramangala</strong> Clinic.
        Are you sure you want to switch clinics?
      </p>
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__continue" data-kal-facility-switch-clinic>Change Clinic</button>
      <button type="button" class="kal-facility-switch-modal__secondary" data-kal-facility-switch-online>Book an online slot</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Calendar modal for Slot Picker's date picker — rebuilt after being
    fully removed (see kal-booking-flow-step-slot-picker.liquid's own
    comment for why) once the day-strip went fully static. Restrictions
    match the real CMS's staff-side SlotPicker.tsx exactly (see
    kal-booking-flow.js's CALENDAR comment for the specific constants/
    citations): today is bookable, strictly past dates are not, and
    nothing beyond today+90 days (MAX_FUTURE_DAYS) is selectable.

    Deliberately a direct child of <dialog>, NOT nested inside
    #kal-booking-flow-content — that div has overflow-y:hidden on
    desktop and the dialog itself has a transform (for centering), which
    makes the dialog the containing block for any position:fixed
    descendant. Once that happens, any overflow-clipping ancestor
    sitting between the fixed element and its containing block clips it
    — nesting the modal inside the scrolling content area would silently
    clip it on desktop, same reasoning as the facility-switch modal above.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="kal-calendar-modal" data-kal-calendar-modal hidden>
    <div class="kal-calendar-modal__backdrop" data-kal-close-calendar></div>
    <div class="kal-calendar-modal__panel">
      <div class="kal-calendar-modal__header">
        <button type="button" class="kal-icon-button" data-kal-calendar-prev aria-label="Previous month">
          {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'chevron-left' -%}
        </button>
        <span class="kal-calendar-modal__month" data-kal-calendar-month>Month Year</span>
        <button type="button" class="kal-icon-button" data-kal-calendar-next aria-label="Next month">
          {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'chevron-right' -%}
        </button>
      </div>
      <div class="kal-calendar-modal__weekdays">
        <span>S</span><span>M</span><span>T</span><span>W</span><span>T</span><span>F</span><span>S</span>
      </div>
      <div class="kal-calendar-modal__grid" data-kal-calendar-grid></div>
      <button type="button" class="kal-calendar-modal__close" data-kal-close-calendar>Done</button>
    </div>
  </div>

</dialog>
